{"type":"message","id":"04a6a0a9","parentId":"b019e7b3","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:14:59.123Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:5","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# A-101 Demolition Plans - Analysis\n\n## Important Caveat\nThis is a **Demolition Plan** (not a construction/layout plan), so detailed room dimensions are limited. The drawing is also at small scale and relatively low resolution, making many dimensions difficult to read with certainty.\n\n## Drawing Scales\n- **D4: Demolition Plan for Conduit Reinstall** — 1/4\" = 1'-0\"\n- **D7: Emergency Entrance Canopy Roof Plan** — 1/8\" = 1'-0\"\n- **A7: Reflected Ceiling Demolition Plan** — 1/8\" = 1'-0\"\n- **A4: Demolition Plan** — 1/8\" = 1'-0\"\n\n## Dimensions Visible on Drawings\n\nFrom the D4 plan (largest scale, most legible):\n\n| Dimension | Approximate Reading |\n|-----------|-------------------|\n| Horizontal spans along grid | **8'-0\"**, **2'-5\"**, **17'-6 1/2\"** (or similar) |\n| Vertical dimension (left side) | **7'-1 1/4\"** |\n| Other horizontal dims | **36'-0\"** (approximate overall), **3'-0\"**, **5'-0\"** |\n| Dimension near bottom | **2'-1\"** |\n\n## Room Identification\n\nThe five rooms (CART WASH, SECURITY STATION, NYPD SECURITY PICKUP, ENTRANCE VESTIBULE, CART ALCOVE) are **not clearly labeled** on this demolition sheet at this resolution. These rooms likely appear on subsequent A-series sheets (A-102, A-103, etc.) with proper dimensioned floor plans.\n\n## Wall Thicknesses\n\nFrom the demolition legend notes, references are made to:\n- Existing wall construction to be removed \"from floor to structure above\"\n- Metal stud walls referenced at **4\"** and **6\"** typical thicknesses (referenced in keynotes)\n\n## What This Sheet Primarily Shows\n\n- **Limits of architectural demolition** (dashed lines)\n- Existing walls/doors/frames to be removed\n- Existing MEP/plumbing fixtures to be removed"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_008.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052499095}}
{"type":"message","id":"a1e1dad3","parentId":"04a6a0a9","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:15:08.683Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:6","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is **not** a Finish Floor Plan (A-801). This is sheet **A-704.00 - Interior Details**, which shows construction details for storefront and door assemblies:\n\n- **C4**: Detail @ Sliding Door ED-1-06 (3\" = 1'-0\")\n- **C2**: Detail @ Exterior Storefront (3\" = 1'-0\")\n- **A4**: Detail @ Exterior Storefront (3\" = 1'-0\")\n- **A2**: Detail @ Interior Storefront (3\" = 1'-0\")\n\nThe details show HSS posts, ballistic resistant glass storefronts, aluminum enclosures, GYP board partitions, and door frame connections for the **ED Ambulance Bay Addition** project at **H+H Bellevue** (462 1st Avenue, New York, NY 10016).\n\n**No room boundaries, floor finishes, room names (Cart Wash, Security Station, NYPD Security Pickup, Entrance Vestibule, Cart Alcove), dimensions, or area measurements for those spaces are present on this sheet.** The requested information would be found on the actual A-801 Finish Floor Plan sheet."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_024.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052508658}}
{"type":"message","id":"390c3c71","parentId":"a1e1dad3","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:15:16.496Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:7","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is **not** a Door Schedule (A-701). This is sheet **A-501.00 – Reflected Ceiling Plan and Roof Plan** for the H+H Bellevue ED Ambulance Bay Addition project.\n\nThe drawing shows:\n- **Level 1 Enlarged Reflected Ceiling Plan** (A3)\n- **Emergency Entrance Canopy Roof Plan** (A8)\n- Ceiling keynotes, general notes, fixture mounting matrix, ceiling finished legend, and ceiling symbol legend\n\n**No door schedule information is present on this sheet.** To review door numbers, types, sizes, materials (HM vs. AL), glazing, hardware sets, and ballistic ratings, you would need sheet **A-701**, which is not provided here."}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_021.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052516490}}
