{"type":"message","id":"a5bc07ef","parentId":"7c9042d6","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:16:37.654Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:18","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Sheet Information\n\n- **Sheet Number:** A-200.00\n- **Sheet Title:** EXTERIOR COMPONENTS AND BUILDING ENCLOSURE SYSTEMS\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue – ED AMBULANCE BAY ADDITION\n- **Architect:** Array Architects\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Issue:** ISSUED SOLUTION FOR BID\n\n## Drawing Types on Sheet\n\nThis is **not a floor plan** — it contains exterior elevations/axonometric views and building enclosure details:\n\n- **Detail 3:** AXON (axonometric view)\n- **Detail 5:** AXON BUILDING INTERIOR\n- **Detail 6:** AXON BUILDING EXTERIOR\n- **Detail 7:** NON-INSULATED INTERIOR SLIDING DOOR AND STOREFRONT (Scale: 1/4\" = 1'-0\")\n- **Detail 2:** INSULATED EXTERIOR SLIDING DOOR AND STOREFRONT (Scale: 1/4\" = 1'-0\")\n\n## Room Names\n\nThe room names you mentioned (CART WASH, SECURITY STATION, NYPD SECURITY PICKUP, ENTRANCE VESTIBULE, CART ALCOVE) are **not visible** on this sheet. This sheet focuses on exterior enclosure systems rather than interior room layouts.\n\n## Building Enclosure System Schedule\n\nThe sheet includes a detailed schedule with assembly types including:\n- **BES-01 through BES-21** — various ballistic-resistant aluminum sliding glass doors, storefront systems, curtain walls, roof assemblies, and foundation details.\n\n## Scales\n\n- Details 2 and 7: **1/4\" = 1'-0\"**\n- Axonometric views: likely NTS (not to scale)"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_011.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052597649}}
