{"type":"message","id":"85ceb6b1","parentId":"e49f7cd4","timestamp":"2026-02-02T17:17:01.855Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"image:20","toolName":"image","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Sheet Information\n\n- **Project:** H+H Bellevue - ED Ambulance Bay Addition\n- **Sheet Title:** BUILDING SECTION\n- **Project No.:** 6629\n- **Date:** 09/25/25\n- **Architect:** ARRAY Architects\n\n## Section Views on Sheet\n\n1. **E7** - Cart Wash and Canopy Section (1/4\" = 1'-0\")\n2. **C7** - Emergency Department Vestibule South Section (1/4\" = 1'-0\")\n3. **A7** - Ambulance Bay Section (1/4\" = 1'-0\")\n4. **A2** - Cart Wash and Security Area Section (1/4\" = 1'-0\")\n\n## Key Dimensions & Elevations\n\n- **Ground Floor:** 13'-1 1/2\"\n- **Canopy T.O.S.:** 26'-7 1/2\"\n- Room labeled **EMERGENCY**\n- **N.I.C.** (Not In Contract) areas noted\n\n## Room Names Identified\n\n- **EMERGENCY** (large signage on elevation)\n- Cart Wash area (referenced in section E7 and A2)\n- Security Area (referenced in section A2)\n- Emergency Department Vestibule (section C7)\n- Existing Electrical Maintenance Area\n\n## Notable Features\n\n- 2\" high polished zinc wall base\n- Raised door access to electrical maintenance area\n- New bollard\n- New sloped ambulance ramp\n- New slab on grade with waterproofing membrane & rigid extruded polystyrene insulation\n- Ballistic resistant aluminum & glass storefront systems (per elevation keynotes)\n- Existing roof deck to remain\n- New wall with continuous blanket insulation\n\n**Scale:** All sections at **1/4\" = 1'-0\"**"}],"details":{"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-4-5","image":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/blueprint/hhc-bellevue-hospital/drawings/pages/page_013.png","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1770052621849}}
